Add duckdb_fetch_chunk_into: fetch into a caller-owned, reused data chunk

Companion to 0001 (both born from profiling C-API clients against
duckdb-python): duckdb_fetch_chunk allocates and initializes a fresh DataChunk
per call (ChunkRetainedCollection::FetchRaw). On the previous result classes
that allocation was ~33% of a chunk-streaming SELECT's runtime.
duckdb_fetch_chunk_into scans the collection directly into a caller-provided
chunk instead:

  - ChunkRetainedCollection::FetchInto(DataChunk&): the scan behind FetchRaw,
    minus the allocation, sharing the same cursor. FetchRaw now allocates a
    chunk and delegates to it. QueryResult::FetchInto adds Fetch's checks.
  - duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(result, chunk): C wrapper. Checks the chunk's column
    count and every column type against the result (the scan writes with the
    destination's physical layout, so a mismatch would reinterpret data); errors
    are recorded on the result. Streams fall back to Fetch +
    DataChunk::Reference (correct, no allocation win). Results in another
    format (0001) are refused without touching their state.

Note for upstreaming: duckdb.h is generated from api_spec/v1 by capigen; this
patch edits the generated header directly. An upstream PR must add a YAML
definition (unstable lifecycle, extension API offset) and regenerate, plus tests.

diff --git a/src/include/duckdb.h b/src/include/duckdb.h
index 0b9e29e2736..509e08bad3d 100644
--- a/src/include/duckdb.h
+++ b/src/include/duckdb.h
@@ -6717,6 +6717,21 @@ DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_result_type duckdb_result_return_type(duckdb_result result);
  * @return duckdb_data_chunk
  */
 DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_data_chunk duckdb_fetch_chunk(duckdb_result result);
+
+/*!
+Fetches the next data chunk into an existing chunk, reusing its buffers. The chunk must have been created with
+`duckdb_create_data_chunk` using exactly the result's column types (checked; a mismatch is an error). Each call
+overwrites its contents; the caller retains ownership.
+
+For retained results this scans directly into the chunk. Streaming results fall back to fetching and referencing the
+returned buffers. Returns false without data for results produced by `duckdb_pending_prepared_arrow`. On failure the
+error is recorded on the result: check `duckdb_result_error` when this returns false.
+
+* @param result The result to fetch from.
+* @param chunk The caller-owned destination chunk.
+* @return true if a chunk was fetched, false when exhausted or on error.
+*/
+DUCKDB_C_API bool duckdb_fetch_chunk_into(duckdb_result result, duckdb_data_chunk chunk);
 #endif
 
 #if DUCKDB_API_VERSION_AT_LEAST(1, 5, 6)
